# A computed boolean passed as a subscope input — refused

`vlag` is computed by the caller and passed to the subscope's boolean input
`hoog`. A boolean passed as a subscope-input value is declared as a boolean
attribute of the caller, and a computed boolean has no rule that writes such
an attribute: the plugin would write a characteristic attribution on it,
which the verifier refuses (WF-022). The plugin refuses the definition of
`vlag` instead. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input hoog content boolean
  output uitkomst content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition uitkomst equals 1
  exception definition uitkomst under condition hoog consequence equals 2

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grens content integer
  internal vlag content boolean
  kamer scope Kamer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition vlag equals grens > 10
  definition kamer.hoog equals vlag
  definition heffing equals kamer.uitkomst
```
